<title>GERMANY: BASF rises after says Kohap buys Magnetics.</title>
<headline>BASF rises after says Kohap buys Magnetics.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German chemicals firm BASF AG rose sharply on Tuesday after the company said South Korea's Kohap group would be taking over its ailing worldwide magnetic tape unit.</p>
<p>BASF shares jumped up to a day high of 50.25 marks after the news, then fell back a little to trade up 78 pfennigs, or 1.6 percent, at 50.04 marks.</p>
<p>BASF said in a statement that the consideration for the acquisition was not being revealed.</p>
<p>Magnetics, one of the world's best known tape brands, posted sales of 1.5 billion marks last year and employs 3,700 workers, but had been posting losses for some time.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
